            <ArticleTitle>[Boerhaave syndrome. Differential diagnosis in acute chest pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous perforation of the esophagus (Boerhaave syndrome) is a rare diagnosis in acute thoracic or epigastric pain. We present the case of a swiftly diagnosed and successfully treated rupture. Apart from pathophysiology, symptoms and diagnosis, the differential diagnosis and therapeutic options are discussed in more detail.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
